COMMAND: analyze_atpg_testability
==================================================
  analyze_atpg_testability: performs ATPG analysis of the design in either assumed scan or fullscan test modes 

Usage: analyze_atpg_testability [-library <string>] [-atpg_options <string>] [-build_model_options <string>] [-build_testmode_options <string>] [-build_faultmodel_options <string>]
           -directory <string> [-atpg_log <string>] [-fault_sample_size <integer>] [<design>]

    [-library <string>]:
        list of Verilog Structural files for the library, e.g. "file1 file2" 
    [-atpg_options <string>]:
        extra options for running atpg (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-build_model_options <string>]:
        extra options for building model (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-build_testmode_options <string>]:
        extra options for building testmode (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-build_faultmodel_options <string>]:
        extra options for building fault model (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    -directory <string>:
        work directory name 
    [-atpg_log <string>]:
        Modus log file name (default: <directory>/atpg.log) 
    [-fault_sample_size <integer>]:
        maximum number of faults in a partition (default: 20000, for full atpg: -1) 
    [<design>]:
        top-level design to perform test analysis on 

==================================================
COMMAND: analyze_scan_compressibility
==================================================
  analyze_scan_compressibility: performs a scan-based compressibility analysis of the design and produces actual compression results for each compression setting 

Usage: analyze_scan_compressibility [-scanins <integer>+] [-scanouts <integer>+] [-channel_lengths <integer>+] -library <string> [-decompressor <string>] [-compression_method <string>]
           [-compressor <string>] [-mask <string>] [-fault_sample_ratio <float>] [-ratios <integer>+] [-directory <string>] [-delay] [-dont_run_atpg] [-min_scanned_flop_percentage <integer>]
           [-verbose] [-build_model_options <string>] [-build_testmode_options <string>] [-build_faultmodel_options <string>] [-atpg_options <string>] [-serial_misr_read]
           [-verify_test_structures_options <string>] [<design>]

    [-scanins <integer>+]:
        number of top level scan I/O (number of chains assumed in design) 
    [-scanouts <integer>+]:
        number of top level scan out ports 
    [-channel_lengths <integer>+]:
        length of compression channels 
    -library <string>:
        list of Verilog Structural files for the library, e.g. "file1 file2" 
    [-decompressor <string>]:
        decompression type 'broadcast' or 'xor' (default is 'xor') 
    [-compression_method <string>]:
        compression method 'compress_scan_chains' or 'add_test_compression' (default is 'add_test_compression') 
    [-compressor <string>]:
        compression type 'xor', 'misr', or 'mimic_bidi_misr' (default is 'xor') 
    [-mask <string>]:
        masking type 'wide0', 'wide1', 'wide2' or 'none' (default is wide1) 
    [-fault_sample_ratio <float>]:
        percentage of faults used to estimate the test coverage (default: 100.0, valid values 100.0 or between 0.01 and 50.0) 
    [-ratios <integer>+]:
        list of compression ratio options (default is "20 50 100" for 'compress_scan_chains' flow) 
    [-directory <string>]:
        temp directory to run atpg (default is './asc)' 
    [-delay]:
        analyze dynamic faults 
    [-dont_run_atpg]:
        dont run atpg, only insert compression 
    [-min_scanned_flop_percentage <integer>]:
        scan flop limit (default is '95') 
    [-verbose]:
        show all messages and warnings 
    [-build_model_options <string>]:
        extra options for building model (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-build_testmode_options <string>]:
        extra options for building testmode (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-build_faultmodel_options <string>]:
        extra options for building fault model (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-atpg_options <string>]:
        extra options for ATPG (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-serial_misr_read]:
        include support for reading the MISR bits serially through the scan data pins 
    [-verify_test_structures_options <string>]:
        extra options for verifying test structures (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [<design>]:
        analyze scan compress for this top design 

