==================================================
COMMAND: check_cpf
==================================================
  check_cpf: checks the validity of the CPF rules against the design 

Usage: check_cpf [-debug] [-run_dir <string>] [-detail] [-isolation] [-level_shifter] [-retention] [-all] [-continue_on_error] [-license <string>] [-pre_read <string>] [-pre_exit <string>]
           [-generated] [-tcl] [-lp_only] [-design <string>] [> file]

    [-debug]:
        debug mode 
    [-run_dir <string>]:
        where to create the temporary CLP run directory 
    [-detail]:
        generate detailed report 
    [-isolation]:
        generate only isolation rule related violations 
    [-level_shifter]:
        generate only level shifter rule related violations 
    [-retention]:
        generate only state retention rule related violations 
    [-all]:
        generate all rule related violations. 
    [-continue_on_error]:
        whether to continue on low power rule check errors. This is not enabled by default 
    [-license <string>]:
        CLP license to be used 
    [-pre_read <string>]:
        an extra dofile to be source'd from dofile right before reading library/design 
    [-pre_exit <string>]:
        an extra dofile to be source'd from dofile right before 'exit' 
    [-generated]:
        use current state of design to perform CPF checks 
    [-tcl]:
        run CLP in TCL mode 
    [-lp_only]:
        report LP related error/warning only. This is the default 
    [-design <string>]:
        specify design module in case of multiple top modules 

==================================================
COMMAND: check_design
==================================================
  check_design: reports information on design state 

Usage: check_design [-undriven] [-unloaded] [-unloaded_comb] [-multiple_driver] [-unresolved] [-constant] [-through_tie_cell] [-feedthrough] [-assigns] [-all] [-preserved] [-physical_only]
           [-logical_only] [-lib_lef_consistency] [-report_scan_pins] [-skip_scan_pins] [-skip_async_pins] [-vname] [-threshold_fanout <integer>] [-only_user_hierarchy] [-long_module_name]
           [-combo_loops] [-status] [<design>] [> file]

    [-undriven]:
        reports undriven ports and pins 
    [-unloaded]:
        reports the unloaded ports and sequential elements (flops and latches) 
    [-unloaded_comb]:
        reports the unloaded comb elements 
    [-multiple_driver]:
        reports multidriven ports and pins 
    [-unresolved]:
        reports the unresolved references and empty modules 
    [-constant]:
        reports the constant pins, ports in the design 
    [-through_tie_cell]:
        reports the constant pins, ports in the design through tie cell 
    [-feedthrough]:
        reports feedthrough modules in the design 
    [-assigns]:
        reports assign statements from the design 
    [-all]:
        report all information 
    [-preserved]:
        reports all preserved instances in the design 
    [-physical_only]:
        report all instances linked to physical only libcells 
    [-logical_only]:
        report all instances linked to logical only libcells 
    [-lib_lef_consistency]:
        reports all the lib-lef inconsistencies 
    [-report_scan_pins]:
        reports all the scan pins also during checks 
    [-skip_scan_pins]:
        skips the scan pins during checks 
    [-skip_async_pins]:
        skips the async pins during checks 
    [-vname]:
        reports only 'vnames of objects' 
    [-threshold_fanout <integer>]:
        reports only the undriven and constant pins with fanout value equal to and above the specified threshold 
    [-only_user_hierarchy]:
        report only user created hierarchies 
    [-long_module_name]:
        report the subdesigns whose name is greater than 1.5k 
    [-combo_loops]:
        returns 1 if combinational cycle detected, 0 by default 
    [-status]:
        returns the status, 1 for any reported instances, 0 by default 
    [<design>]:
        specify the design name for which the check netlist is to be performed 

