==================================================
COMMAND: compress_scan_chains
==================================================
  compress_scan_chains: inserts scan compression logic into actual (existing) scan chains 

Usage: compress_scan_chains [-ratio <integer>] [-chains <actual_scan_chain>+] [-channel_length <integer>] [-decompressor <string>] [-compressor <string>] [-mask <string>]
           [-mask_sharing_ratio <integer>] [-auto_create] [-master_control <test_signal>] [-compression_enable <test_signal>] [-spread_enable <test_signal>]
           [-misr_reset_enable <test_signal>] [-misr_reset_clock <test_signal>] [-misr_clock <pin|hpin|port>] [-misr_shift_enable <test_signal>] [-misr_bypass <test_signal>]
           [-mask_load <test_signal>] [-mask_enable <test_signal>+] [-mask_clock <pin|hpin|port>] [-mask_or_misr_sdi <pin|hpin|port>] [-mask_or_misr_sdo <pin|hpin|port>] [-shared_output]
           [-create_mask_or_misr_chain] [-preview] [-allow_shared_clocks] [-inside <inst|hinst>] [-apply_timing_constraints] [-write_timing_constraints <string>] [-timing_mode_names <mode>+]
           [-power_aware] [-misr_read <test_signal>] [-dont_exploit_inout_scan_io] [-use_all_scan_ios_unidirectionally] [-serial_misr_read] [-misr_obs <test_signal>]
           [-target_period <integer>] [-jtag_control_instruction <jtag_instruction>] [-allow_multiple_jtag_control] [-share_mask_enable_with_scan_in] [-low_pin_compression]
           [-low_pin_comp_control <test_signal>] [-shift_enable <test_signal>] [-gate_shared_compression_clock] [-smartscan_ratio <integer>] [-smartscan_serial_only]
           [-smartscan_enable <test_signal>] [-smartscan_parallel_access <test_signal>] [-smartscan_no_update_stage] [-smartscan_pulse_width_multiplier <integer>]
           [-smartscan_serial_scan_ins <pin|hpin|port>+] [<design>]

    [-ratio <integer>]:
        compression ratio used to determine the length of the internal scan channels 
    [-chains <actual_scan_chain>+]:
        name(s) of the actual scan chain(s) to be compressed (default: compress all actual scan chains) 
    [-channel_length <integer>]:
        maximum length of the internal scan channels 
    [-decompressor <string>]:
        type of decompression logic to be built, 'broadcast' or 'xor' (default: broadcast) 
    [-compressor <string>]:
        type of compression logic to be built, 'xor', 'smartscan_xor', 'misr' or 'hybrid' (default: xor) 
    [-mask <string>]:
        specifies to insert masking logic of type 'wide0', 'wide1', or 'wide2' (default is not to insert masking logic) 
    [-mask_sharing_ratio <integer>]:
        number of internal scan channels sharing a mask register 
    [-auto_create]:
        automatically creates the necessary compression control signals as top-level ports 
    [-master_control <test_signal>]:
        test mode signal used to gate the compression enable and other signals used for compression 
    [-compression_enable <test_signal>]:
        test signal used to enable compression 
    [-spread_enable <test_signal>]:
        test signal used to select test data from the xor-spreader network (required for '-decompressor xor') 
    [-misr_reset_enable <test_signal>]:
        test signal used to reset the MISR registers (required for '-compressor misr') 
    [-misr_reset_clock <test_signal>]:
        use this test_signal to asynchronously reset the MISR registers (allows misr_clock to be shared with existing test clock) 
    [-misr_clock <pin|hpin|port>]:
        use this clock pin to control the MISR registers (required for '-compressor misr') 
    [-misr_shift_enable <test_signal>]:
        test signal used as shift enable for MISR registers 
    [-misr_bypass <test_signal>]:
        test signal used to bypass the MISR logic (required for '-compressor hybrid') 
    [-mask_load <test_signal>]:
        test signal which enables loading of the mask data into the mask registers 
    [-mask_enable <test_signal>+]:
        test signal which controls whether the mask bits should be applied during current scan cycle 
    [-mask_clock <pin|hpin|port>]:
        use this clock pin to control the mask registers 
    [-mask_or_misr_sdi <pin|hpin|port>]:
        scan-data input pin or port used for the dedicated mask/misr scan chain 
    [-mask_or_misr_sdo <pin|hpin|port>]:
        scan-data output pin or port used for the dedicated mask/misr scan chain 
    [-shared_output]:
        whether the scan-data output pin/port of the dedicated mask/misr chain is shared with a functional connection 
    [-create_mask_or_misr_chain]:
        add mask and misr registers to a separate chain 
    [-preview]:
        reports what would be done, but does not modify the netlist 
    [-allow_shared_clocks]:
        allows the misr or mask clock to be shared with an existing full-scan test clock 
    [-inside <inst|hinst>]:
        instance in which to instantiate the compression logic 
    [-apply_timing_constraints]:
        apply the timing constraints for compression on the design 
    [-write_timing_constraints <string>]:
        write the timing constraints for compression to a file 
    [-timing_mode_names <mode>+]:
        timing mode(s) in which to apply timing constraints in case multi mode synthesis is being done 
    [-power_aware]:
        break sub-chains on power domain boundaries 
    [-misr_read <test_signal>]:
        test signal to configure the bidir pads in bidirectional compression 
    [-dont_exploit_inout_scan_io]:
        do not use bidirectional scan compression 
    [-use_all_scan_ios_unidirectionally]:
        do not use bidirectional scan compression 
    [-serial_misr_read]:
        include support for reading the MISR bits serially through the scan data pins 
    [-misr_obs <test_signal>]:
        test signal used to select Serial MISR Read 
    [-target_period <integer>]:
        optimize the compression macro to operate at this target clock period (picoseconds) (defaults to the test_clock period) 
    [-jtag_control_instruction <jtag_instruction>]:
        the JTAG instruction which selects the TDR to control the compression macro 
    [-allow_multiple_jtag_control]:
        allows the insertion of multiple JTAG controlled compression macros 
    [-share_mask_enable_with_scan_in]:
        share the mask enable pin with scan in pin 
    [-low_pin_compression]:
        low pin count compression 
    [-low_pin_comp_control <test_signal>]:
        low pin count compression control pin 
    [-shift_enable <test_signal>]:
        user specified shift enable for low pin count compression (default shift enable is used by default) 
    [-gate_shared_compression_clock]:
        gate the existing mask clock loads 
    [-smartscan_ratio <integer>]:
        length of the deserializer and serializer registers 
    [-smartscan_serial_only]:
        only serial smartscan interface 
    [-smartscan_enable <test_signal>]:
        enables smartscan 
    [-smartscan_parallel_access <test_signal>]:
        enables parallel access of scan-ins 
    [-smartscan_no_update_stage]:
        update registers not to be added 
    [-smartscan_pulse_width_multiplier <integer>]:
        multiplier to widen the clock pulse 
    [-smartscan_serial_scan_ins <pin|hpin|port>+]:
        scan-in(s) of actual scan chain(s) to be used for smartscan serial access 
    [<design>]:
        compress scan chains for this top design 

==================================================
COMMAND: connect
==================================================
  connect: connects a list of pins/ports/subports to each other, possibly at a different hierarchy level 

Usage: connect [-constant <integer>] ((null) <constant|hport|port|pg_pin|pin|hpin>+)+ [-net <net>] [-hnet <hnet>] [-net_name <string>] [-in_prefix <string>] [-out_prefix <string>]

    [-constant <integer>]:
        connect the object to a constant 
    <constant|hport|port|pg_pin|pin|hpin>+:
        list of objects to connect 
    [-net <net>]:
        the net object to be used for the connections 
    [-hnet <hnet>]:
        the hnet object to be used for the connections 
    [-net_name <string>]:
        name for the net connection 
    [-in_prefix <string>]:
        prefix to be used for naming new input ports 
    [-out_prefix <string>]:
        prefix to be used for naming new output ports 

==================================================
COMMAND: connect_cgic_test_pins_controlling_wrapper_cells
==================================================
  connect_cgic_test_pins_controlling_wrapper_cells: identify CGICs for shared wrapper cells and connect their test enable pins 

Usage: connect_cgic_test_pins_controlling_wrapper_cells [-test_enable <pin|hpin|port>] [-verbose] [-genus_cgics_only] [-dont_retain_test_enable_connection] [<design|inst|hinst>] [> file]

    [-test_enable <pin|hpin|port>]:
        connect the test pin of the clock gates controlling shared wrapper cells to this pin|port 
    [-verbose]:
        print a table showing the leaf clock gates and the shared wrapper flops controlled by the clock gates 
    [-genus_cgics_only]:
        identify only Genus inserted clock gates 
    [-dont_retain_test_enable_connection]:
        retains the already connected logic to TE pins for both RTL and Genus inserted CGICs 
    [<design|inst|hinst>]:
        identify cgics on this module or instance 

==================================================
COMMAND: connect_dft_top_level
==================================================
  connect_dft_top_level: connects the top-level Test Interconnect Macro to the cores in the Heirarchical Test flow. 

Usage: connect_dft_top_level [-scan_in_pipeline_depth <integer>] [-scan_out_pipeline_depth <integer>] [-mask_enable_pipeline_depth <integer>] [<design>]

    [-scan_in_pipeline_depth <integer>]:
        length of the scan input pipeline 
    [-scan_out_pipeline_depth <integer>]:
        length of the scan output pipeline 
    [-mask_enable_pipeline_depth <integer>]:
        length of the mask enable pipeline 
    [<design>]:
        connects the top level test interconnect macro 

==================================================
COMMAND: connect_opcg_segments
==================================================
  connect_opcg_segments: connects OPCG segments into actual scan chains 

Usage: connect_opcg_segments [-preview] [-chains <actual_scan_chain>+] [-use_ports_for_side_scan_connections <port>+] [-side_scan_only] [<design>]

    [-preview]:
        report what would be done, but not connect 
    [-chains <actual_scan_chain>+]:
        chains to prepend OPCG segments to 
    [-use_ports_for_side_scan_connections <port>+]:
        ports to connect the side scan chains to (most applicable to RTL inserted compression flows) 
    [-side_scan_only]:
        connect OPCG side scan chains only (OPCG segments are already connected in chains) 
    [<design>]:
        connect OPCG segments for this top module 

==================================================
COMMAND: connect_scan_chains
==================================================
  connect_scan_chains: connects scan registers and segments which pass DFT rules into scan chains 

Usage: connect_scan_chains [-preview] [-elements <scan_segment|inst|hinst>+] [-chains <scan_chain>+] [-auto_create_chains] [-incremental] [-dont_exceed_min_number_of_scan_chains] [-pack]
           [-physical] [-create_empty_chains] [-power_domain <power_domain>+] [-dft_cfg_mode <dft_configuration_mode>] [-cluster_aggressively_high] [-zipper_stitch] [-include_opcg_segments]
           [-update_placement] [-keep_connected_shift_enable] [-partitions <string>] [<design>]

    [-preview]:
        report what would be done, but do not connect 
    [-elements <scan_segment|inst|hinst>+]:
        instances and segments to be connected 
    [-chains <scan_chain>+]:
        scan chains to be used 
    [-auto_create_chains]:
        automatically create new scan chains - as needed 
    [-incremental]:
        connect chains in incremental mode 
    [-dont_exceed_min_number_of_scan_chains]:
        use the exact same number of scan chains as specified by 'dft_min_number_of_scan_chains' attribute 
    [-pack]:
        pack scan chains to their maximum limit instead of balancing the chains 
    [-physical]:
        connects scan chains on the basis of physical information 
    [-create_empty_chains]:
        create empty chains if required 
    [-power_domain <power_domain>+]:
        power domains of flops to consider for connect scan 
    [-dft_cfg_mode <dft_configuration_mode>]:
        configuration mode in which to connect scan chains 
    [-cluster_aggressively_high]:
        aggressively cluster the flops and segments into scan chains 
    [-zipper_stitch]:
        perform zipper stitching of abstract segments 
    [-include_opcg_segments]:
        includes the opcg segments as part of the scan chains 
    [-update_placement]:
        update placement of any DFT logic added during scan_chain connection 
    [-keep_connected_shift_enable]:
        retain any existing connection to shift enable signals 
    [-partitions <string>]:
        list of partitions 
    [<design>]:
        connect scan chains for this top module 

==================================================
COMMAND: connect_serial_scan_chains
==================================================
  connect_serial_scan_chains: concatenates actual scan chains for a specific DFT mode of operation 

Usage: connect_serial_scan_chains [-preview] -chains <actual_scan_chain>+ [-dft_cfg_mode <dft_configuration_mode>] -name <string> [<design>]

    [-preview]:
        report what would be done, but do not concatenate 
    -chains <actual_scan_chain>+:
        actual scan chains to be concatenated 
    [-dft_cfg_mode <dft_configuration_mode>]:
        configuration mode in which to concatenate the scan chains 
    -name <string>:
        name of the concatenated chain 
    [<design>]:
        connect scan chains for this top module 

