==================================================
COMMAND: create_floorplan
==================================================
  create_floorplan: specify design floorplan 

Usage: create_floorplan [-core_margin_by <string>] [-die_size_by_io_height <string>] [-flip <string>] [-floorplan_origin <string>] [-match_to_site] [-no_resize] [-no_snap_to_grid]
           [-overlap_same_site_row]
           [ -box_size <float>+ |
             -core_size <float>+ |
             -die_size <float>+ |
             -core_density_size <float>+ |
             -stdcell_density_size <float>+ |
             -keep_shape_density <float> ]
           [ -site <string> |
             -site_only <string> ]

    [-core_margin_by <string>]:
        core margin to io or die <io|die> 
    [-die_size_by_io_height <string>]:
        use max or min io height for inital die size <min|max> 
    [-flip <string>]:
        to flip rows <n|s|f> 
    [-floorplan_origin <string>]:
        set fplan origin at center or llcorner 
    [-match_to_site]:
        floorplan boxes is multiple times of io site or core site's width 
    [-no_resize]:
        check if need do floorplan if everthing is same 
    [-no_snap_to_grid]:
        do not change input floorplan boxes 
    [-overlap_same_site_row]:
        allow same site row overlapping 
    -box_size <float>+:
        specify all 2 boxes of floorplan <die_box core_box> 
    -core_size <float>+:
        by core size and core to edge <w h left bottom right top> 
    -die_size <float>+:
        by DIE size and core to edge <w h left bottom right top> 
    -core_density_size <float>+:
        by aspectratio, density and core to edge <aspectratio [rowdensity [left bottom right top]]> 
    -stdcell_density_size <float>+:
        by aspectratio, density and core to edge <aspectratio rowdensity left bottom right top> 
    -keep_shape_density <float>:
        target utilization after resize 
    -site <string>:
        default tech site name 
    -site_only <string>:
        default tech site name, create row for the site 

