==================================================
COMMAND: create_flow_step
==================================================
  create_flow_step: create a flow step that will be cached in the database 

Usage: create_flow_step -name <string> [-copy <string>] [-begin <string>] [-end <string>] [-check <string>] [-write_db] [-skip_metric] [-owner <string>] [-exclude_time_metric]
           [-categories <string>] [<string>]

    -name <string>:
        name of the step 
    [-copy <string>]:
        copy the named step to this step 
    [-begin <string>]:
        tcl code to always execute at the start of this step 
    [-end <string>]:
        tcl code to always execute at the end of this step 
    [-check <string>]:
        tcl code to run specific tcl checks 
    [-write_db]:
        automatically write a db file after step completion 
    [-skip_metric]:
        disables automatically saving metrics once the step is complete 
    [-owner <string>]:
        owner of this step 
    [-exclude_time_metric]:
        do not include cpu and wall time of this step in any parent steps 
    [-categories <string>]:
        metric categories to calculate for this flow step 
    [<string>]:
        tcl proc code 

==================================================
COMMAND: create_generated_clock
==================================================

Usage: create_generated_clock [-name <string>] [-comment <string>] [-domain <string>] [-add] -source <pin|hpin|port> [-master_clock <clock>] [-divide_by <integer>] [-multiply_by <integer>]
           [-duty_cycle <float>] [-invert] [-edges <integer>+] [-edge_shift <float>+] [-apply_inverted <object>+] [-combinational] <pin|hpin|port>+

    [-name <string>]:
        name of the generated clock 
    [-comment <string>]:
        comment to be tagged with this command 
    [-domain <string>]:
        name of the clock domain for the clock 
    [-add]:
        should the clock sources add or overwrite 
    -source <pin|hpin|port>:
        master_pin 
    [-master_clock <clock>]:
        master clock 
    [-divide_by <integer>]:
        divide_factor 
    [-multiply_by <integer>]:
        multiply_factor 
    [-duty_cycle <float>]:
        percentage high pulse for multiply factor (between 0.0 and 100.0) 
    [-invert]:
        should we invert the resulting waveform 
    [-edges <integer>+]:
        list of clock edge identifiers 
    [-edge_shift <float>+]:
        list of clock edge shift values 
    [-apply_inverted <object>+]:
        where to apply the inverted clock waveform 
    [-combinational]:
        source latency includes the logic where the master clock propagates 
    <pin|hpin|port>+:
        where to apply the clock 

