==================================================
COMMAND: define_scan_abstract_segment
==================================================
  define_scan_abstract_segment: defines a scan segment whose content is to be abstracted for scan chain connection 

Usage: define_scan_abstract_segment [-name <string>] [-module <module>] [-instance <inst|hinst>] [-lib_cell <lib_cell>+] -sdi <string> -sdo <string> -clock_port <string> [-rise] [-fall]
           [-tail_clock_port <string>] [-tail_edge_rise] [-tail_edge_fall] [-off_state <string>] [-tail_clock_off_state <string>] [-shift_enable_port <string>]
           [-cg_shift_enable_port <string>]+ [-active <string>] [-cg_shift_enable_active <string>]+ [-connected_shift_enable] [-test_mode_port <string>]+ [-test_mode_active <string>]+
           [-other_clock_port <string>]+ [-other_clock_edge <string>]+ -length <integer> [-skew_safe] [-skew_latch] [-skew_flop] [-inversion] [-tail_inversion] [-head_skew_safe]
           [-dft_cfg_mode <dft_configuration_mode>]

    [-name <string>]:
        name of the segment 
    [-module <module>]:
        module where the abstract segment resides 
    [-instance <inst|hinst>]:
        instance of the module where the abstract segment resides 
    [-lib_cell <lib_cell>+]:
        library cell where the abstract segment resides 
    -sdi <string>:
        scan data in pin/port for the segment 
    -sdo <string>:
        scan data out pin/port for the segment 
    -clock_port <string>:
        clock port driving the flops in the segment 
    [-rise]:
        the clock in -clock_port option triggers on the rising edge 
    [-fall]:
        the clock in -clock_port option triggers on the falling edge 
    [-tail_clock_port <string>]:
        clock port driving the flops at the tail of abstract segment (if different from -clock_port) 
    [-tail_edge_rise]:
        the clock in -tail_clock_port option triggers on the rising edge (default) 
    [-tail_edge_fall]:
        the clock in -tail_clock_port option triggers on the falling edge 
    [-off_state <string>]:
        the off state of the clock in -clock_port for abstract segments in clocked LSSD scan style 
    [-tail_clock_off_state <string>]:
        the off state of the clock in -tail_clock_port for abstract segments in clocked LSSD scan style (if different from -off_state) 
    [-shift_enable_port <string>]:
        shift enable port connected to the flops in abstract segment 
    [-cg_shift_enable_port <string>]:
        shift enable port connected to the flops in abstract segment 
    [-active <string>]:
        active value of shift_enable port {high|low} 
    [-cg_shift_enable_active <string>]:
        active value of shift_enable port {high|low} 
    [-connected_shift_enable]:
        assume the shift enable of the segment is already connected 
    [-test_mode_port <string>]:
        test mode port connected to flops in abstract segment 
    [-test_mode_active <string>]:
        active value of the test mode port {high|low} 
    [-other_clock_port <string>]:
        other clock ports used for the abstract segment 
    [-other_clock_edge <string>]:
        the clock in -other_clock_port options triggers on the rising edge (default) 
    -length <integer>:
        sequential length of the segment 
    [-skew_safe]:
        the segment has an anti-skew element at its end 
    [-skew_latch]:
        the segment has an anti-skew latch at its end 
    [-skew_flop]:
        the segment has an anti-skew flop at its end 
    [-inversion]:
        an inversion exists at the scan in pin of the segment 
    [-tail_inversion]:
        an inversion exists at the scan out pin of the segment 
    [-head_skew_safe]:
        the segment has an anti skew element at its head 
    [-dft_cfg_mode <dft_configuration_mode>]:
        configuration mode in which to connect scan chains 

==================================================
COMMAND: define_scan_chain
==================================================
  define_scan_chain: defines a scan chain 

Usage: define_scan_chain [-name <string>] [-sdi <hport|port|pin|hpin>] [-hookup_pin_sdi <pin|hpin>] [-sdo <hport|port|pin|hpin>] [-hookup_pin_sdo <pin|hpin>] [-analyze] [-create_ports]
           [-shared_output] [-shared_input] [-non_shared_output] [-shared_select <test_signal>] [-shift_enable <test_signal>] [-head <scan_segment>] [-tail <scan_segment>]
           [-body <scan_segment>] [-complete] [-domain <test_clock_domain>] [-edge <string>] [-max_length <integer>] [-cfg_pad <test_signal>] [-terminal_lockup <string>] [-dont_overlay]

    [-name <string>]:
        name of the chain 
    [-sdi <hport|port|pin|hpin>]:
        name of the scan-data input pin/port of the chain 
    [-hookup_pin_sdi <pin|hpin>]:
        core side hookup pin for SDI 
    [-sdo <hport|port|pin|hpin>]:
        name of the scan-data output pin/port of the chain 
    [-hookup_pin_sdo <pin|hpin>]:
        core side hookup pin for SDO 
    [-analyze]:
        analyze an existing scan chain 
    [-create_ports]:
        create SDI/SDO ports if they do not exist 
    [-shared_output]:
        whether the scan-data output pin/port is shared with a functional connection 
    [-shared_input]:
        whether the scan-data input pin/port is shared with a functional connection 
    [-non_shared_output]:
        whether the scan-data output pin/port is not shared with a functional connection 
    [-shared_select <test_signal>]:
        name of the test signal for the shared out mux 
    [-shift_enable <test_signal>]:
        name of the shift-enable signal for chain 
    [-head <scan_segment>]:
        name of user-defined segment to be placed at the head of chain 
    [-tail <scan_segment>]:
        name of user-defined segment to be placed at the tail of chain 
    [-body <scan_segment>]:
        name of user-defined segment to be placed in the middle (if head and tail specified) or anywhere in chain 
    [-complete]:
        indicates the included segments define a complete chain 
    [-domain <test_clock_domain>]:
        name of test-clock domain (see 'define_dft test_clock' command) 
    [-edge <string>]:
        use only flip-flops active on this edge {rise|fall} 
    [-max_length <integer>]:
        length of chain (when '-complete' option is not used) 
    [-cfg_pad <test_signal>]:
        configure connected pads using the test-signal 
    [-terminal_lockup <string>]:
        type of lockup element inserted at the tail end of chain ('level_sensitive' or 'edge_sensitive') 
    [-dont_overlay]:
        do not overlay the user defined segments onto the actual scan chain when specified with the -analyzed option 

