==================================================
COMMAND: define_shift_enable
==================================================
  define_shift_enable: defines a shift enable signal 

Usage: define_shift_enable [-name <string>] -active <string> [-create_port] [-default] [-cfg_pad <test_signal>] [-ideal] [-hookup_pin <pin|hpin>] [-hookup_polarity <string>] <port|pin|hpin>
           [-design <design>] [-lec_value <string>]

    [-name <string>]:
        test signal name 
    -active <string>:
        active value (high|low) 
    [-create_port]:
        create port if it does not exist 
    [-default]:
        make this the default shift enable signal 
    [-cfg_pad <test_signal>]:
        configure connected pad using the test-signal 
    [-ideal]:
        sets the ideal network true 
    [-hookup_pin <pin|hpin>]:
        consider this as the core side hookup pin 
    [-hookup_polarity <string>]:
        polarity of signal (inverted | non_inverted) 
    <port|pin|hpin>:
        driving port or pin 
    [-design <design>]:
        top-block (required if there are multiple top designs) 
    [-lec_value <string>]:
        specifies lec value or string for the test signal, '0', '1', 'no_value' or 'auto' (default: auto) 

