==================================================
COMMAND: define_test_clock
==================================================
  define_test_clock: defines a test clock 

Usage: define_test_clock [-name <string>] [-domain <string>] [-period <delay in picoseconds>] [-divide_period <integer>] [-rise <integer>] [-divide_rise <integer>] [-fall <integer>]
           [-divide_fall <integer>] [-controllable] [-controllable_from <port>] [-function {test_clock|dft_clock|compressor_clock}] [-cfg_pad <test_signal>] [-design <design>]
           [-hookup_pin <pin|hpin>] [-hookup_polarity <string>] [-create_port <string>] [<pin|hpin|port>+]

    [-name <string>]:
        clock name 
    [-domain <string>]:
        domain name (default is assigning each clock to a different domain) 
    [-period <delay in picoseconds>]:
        period interval in picoseconds (default is 50000.000000) 
    [-divide_period <integer>]:
        clock periods per interval (default is 1) to create a 100MHz clock use '-period 10000' to create a 300MHz clock use '-period 10000 -divide_period 3' (the period is 10000/3 
        picoseconds) 
    [-rise <integer>]:
        rise period fraction numerator (default is 50) 
    [-divide_rise <integer>]:
        rise period fraction denominator (default is 100) 
    [-fall <integer>]:
        fall period fraction numerator (default is 90) 
    [-divide_fall <integer>]:
        fall period fraction denominator (default 100) the default is a clock that rises at 50% of the clock period and falls at 90% of the clock period to create a waveform that rises 
        after 20% of the period and falls after 80% of the period use '-rise 20 -fall 80' to create a waveform that falls after 1/3 of the period and rises after 2/3 of the period use -fall 
        1 -divide_fall 3 -rise 2 -divide_rise 3 
    [-controllable]:
        whether the clock is controllable in test mode 
    [-controllable_from <port>]:
        source hookup where the clock is controllable from 
    [-function {test_clock|dft_clock|compressor_clock}]:
        function of the test clock (default: test_clock) 
    [-cfg_pad <test_signal>]:
        configure connected pad using the test-signal 
    [-design <design>]:
        top-block (required if there are multiple top designs) 
    [-hookup_pin <pin|hpin>]:
        consider this as the core side hookup pin 
    [-hookup_polarity <string>]:
        polarity of signal (inverted | non_inverted) 
    [-create_port <string>]:
        create port if it does not exist 
    [<pin|hpin|port>+]:
        source ports/pins 

