==================================================

Usage: get_designs [-quiet] [-filter <string>] <string>

    [-quiet]:
        ignored option 
    [-filter <string>]:
        filter based on DC expression 
    <string>:
        design names 

==================================================
COMMAND: get_fanin
==================================================
  get_fanin: traces fanin from a pin or port 

Usage: get_fanin [-structural] [-floating_hport] [-stop_at_seqs] [-trace_through_combinational] [-ignore_broken_timing_paths] [-min_logic_depth <integer>] [-max_logic_depth <integer>]
           [-min_pin_depth <integer>] [-max_pin_depth <integer>] [-startpoints] [-gui] <port|pg_pin|pin|hpin|hport|hnet|net>+

    [-structural]:
        does a structural trace instead of timing-based 
    [-floating_hport]:
        only used with structural trace.Returns only floating hport 
    [-stop_at_seqs]:
        stops structural trace at sequential elements 
    [-trace_through_combinational]:
        only used with structural trace. With this option it will trace through timing model combinational libcells 
    [-ignore_broken_timing_paths]:
        ignore broken timing paths in design and follow pure structural fanin flow 
    [-min_logic_depth <integer>]:
        only returns pins at least this many logic levels backward 
    [-max_logic_depth <integer>]:
        does not return pins more than this many logic levels backward 
    [-min_pin_depth <integer>]:
        only returns pins at least this many pin levels backward 
    [-max_pin_depth <integer>]:
        does not return pins more than this many pin levels backward 
    [-startpoints]:
        only returns timing startpoints 
    [-gui]:
        highlight in physical viewer 
    <port|pg_pin|pin|hpin|hport|hnet|net>+:
        the sink objects 

==================================================
COMMAND: get_fanout
==================================================
  get_fanout: traces fanout from a pin or port 

Usage: get_fanout [-structural] [-floating_hport] [-stop_at_seqs] [-trace_through_combinational] [-ignore_broken_timing_paths] [-endpoints] [-gui] [-min_logic_depth <integer>]
           [-max_logic_depth <integer>] [-min_pin_depth <integer>] [-max_pin_depth <integer>] <port|pg_pin|pin|hpin|hport|hnet|net>+

    [-structural]:
        does a structural trace instead of timing-based 
    [-floating_hport]:
        only used with structural trace.Returns only floating hport 
    [-stop_at_seqs]:
        stops the structural trace at sequential elements 
    [-trace_through_combinational]:
        only used with structural trace. With this option it will trace through timing model combinational libcells 
    [-ignore_broken_timing_paths]:
        ignore broken timing paths in design and follow pure structural fanout flow 
    [-endpoints]:
        only returns timing endpoints 
    [-gui]:
        highlight in physical viewer 
    [-min_logic_depth <integer>]:
        only returns pins at least this many logic levels forward 
    [-max_logic_depth <integer>]:
        does not return pins more than this many logic levels forward 
    [-min_pin_depth <integer>]:
        only returns pins at least this many pin levels forward 
    [-max_pin_depth <integer>]:
        does not return pins more than this many pin levels forward 
    <port|pg_pin|pin|hpin|hport|hnet|net>+:
        the source objects 

