==================================================
COMMAND: read_def
==================================================
  read_def: reads in a DEF file 

Usage: read_def <string> [-convert_sites <string>] [-design <design>] [-fuzzy_match] [-hierarchical] [-incremental] [-ignore_errors] [-no_special_nets] [-no_nets] [-no_vias]
           [-no_physical_pins] [-keep_all_instances] [-keep_filler_cells] [-keep_routed_nets] [-keep_welltap_cells] [-keep_all_physical_cells] [-create_ports] [-add_power_switch]
           [-no_force_fixed]

    <string>:
        DEF file to read 
    [-convert_sites <string>]:
        convert ROW sites 
    [-design <design>]:
        design to annotate DEF info 
    [-fuzzy_match]:
        enable fuzzy name matching 
    [-hierarchical]:
        read hierarchical DEF 
    [-incremental]:
        read incremental DEF for blockages, components, groups, pins, and regions 
    [-ignore_errors]:
        ignore LEF/DEF consistency check errors 
    [-no_special_nets]:
        do not read the SPECIALNETS section 
    [-no_nets]:
        do not read the NETS section 
    [-no_vias]:
        do not read the VIAS section 
    [-no_physical_pins]:
        do not create physical pin for missing PIN 
    [-keep_all_instances]:
        keep all non-netlist instances 
    [-keep_filler_cells]:
        keep physical only filler cells 
    [-keep_routed_nets]:
        keep routed (in addition to fixed/cover) NETS 
    [-keep_welltap_cells]:
        keep physical only welltap cells 
    [-keep_all_physical_cells]:
        keep cells with lib_cell attribute keep_as_physical set 
    [-create_ports]:
        create missing DEF pins (clock, reset, scan, or signal) 
    [-add_power_switch]:
        create power switch in netlist 
    [-no_force_fixed]:
        do not force components to be fixed in hierarchical mode 

