COMMAND: read_dft_abstract_model
==================================================
  read_dft_abstract_model: reads scan abstract model in native or CTL format for top-level scan chain stitching 

Usage: read_dft_abstract_model [-ctl] [-advanced] [-segment_prefix <string>] [-libcell <string>] [-instance <inst|hinst>] [-assume_connected_shift_enable]
           [-use_scan_structures_shift_enable_only] [-override_scan_lib_cell] <string>

    [-ctl]:
        reads in the abstraction model in CTL format 
    [-advanced]:
        set dft_controllable across feedthrough pins specified with the IsConnected keyword in CTL 
    [-segment_prefix <string>]:
        prefix applied to the segment chain name (for third party generated files) 
    [-libcell <string>]:
        libcell of segment 
    [-instance <inst|hinst>]:
        apply the segment to the designated instance 
    [-assume_connected_shift_enable]:
        assume connected shift enable 
    [-use_scan_structures_shift_enable_only]:
        use the shift enable from the ScanStructures block 
    [-override_scan_lib_cell]:
        allow specifying abstract segments on scan flop library cells 
    <string>:
        the file name to be read 

