==================================================
COMMAND: read_vcd
==================================================
  read_vcd: reads in Value Change Dump (VCD) file for power analysis 

Usage: read_vcd [-static] [-scale <string>] [-start_time <float>] [-end_time <float>] [-time_window <float>] [-activity_profile] [-vcd_scope <string>] [-hinst <string>] [-simvision]
           [-write_sst2 <string>] [-nocase] [-scale_to_sdc_frequency] <string>

    [-static]:
        do static VCD analysis 
    [-scale <string>]:
        the scaling factor 
    [-start_time <float>]:
        time in picoseconds at which VCD analysis starts 
    [-end_time <float>]:
        time in picoseconds at which VCD analysis ends 
    [-time_window <float>]:
        period in picoseconds for doing incremental analysis 
    [-activity_profile]:
        monitor switching activity of objects in VCD file 
    [-vcd_scope <string>]:
        the instance for VCD parsing 
    [-hinst <string>]:
        the instance in the design hierarchy corresponding to the instance in the VCD selected for parsing 
    [-simvision]:
        generate SST2 database for running simvision (default false) 
    [-write_sst2 <string>]:
        SST2 database file name for viewing in other waveform viewers 
    [-nocase]:
        ignore the case for finding design objects (default false) 
    [-scale_to_sdc_frequency]:
        scales activities to sdc activities 
    <string>:
        the name of the VCD file 

