==================================================
COMMAND: report_multibit_inferencing
==================================================
  report_multibit_inferencing: prints a multibit inferencing report 

Usage: report_multibit_inferencing [-power] [-lib] [-sequential] [-combinational] [-iso_ls] [-no_header] [-mapping] [-tcl] [-not_merged_summary] [-not_merged_instance_list]
           [-reason_not_merged <string>] [-find_libcell <lib_cell>] [-hinst <inst|hinst>] [-exclude_synchronizer] [<design>] [> file]

    [-power]:
        adds leakage power information 
    [-lib]:
        reports multibit cells available in library,(Do not use design/instance_hier option) 
    [-sequential]:
        reports info only for sequential multibit cells 
    [-combinational]:
        reports info only for combinational multibit cells 
    [-iso_ls]:
        reports info only for iso/ls multibit cells 
    [-no_header]:
        prints the report without header 
    [-mapping]:
        reports the single bit instances mapping with corresponding multibit sequential instance, (> redirection to a file is recommended) 
    [-tcl]:
        generates create_multibit.tcl file which contains list of commands to merge single bit flops individually 
    [-not_merged_summary]:
        reports number of unmerged instances in each category of reason of not merging 
    [-not_merged_instance_list]:
        reports all single bit sequential instances not merged to multibit, (> redirection to a file is recommended) 
    [-reason_not_merged <string>]:
        only reports the instances for specific reason of not merging. use "all" to report all reason instances 
    [-find_libcell <lib_cell>]:
        provides info about the specified libcell 
    [-hinst <inst|hinst>]:
        hierarchical instance name to report multibit_inferencing 
    [-exclude_synchronizer]:
        reports multibit coverage excluding synchronizer 
    [<design>]:
        design to report on 

