==================================================
COMMAND: report_nets
==================================================
  report_nets: prints a nets report 

Usage: report_nets [-hierarchical] [-pin <pin|hpin>+] [-min_fanout <integer>] [-max_fanout <integer>] [-cap_worst <integer>] [-sort <string>] [-flat] [<inst|hinst|hnet>+] [> file]

    [-hierarchical]:
        reports all the nets in the design hierarchy 
    [-pin <pin|hpin>+]:
        reports nets on the given pin name(s) <optional> 
    [-min_fanout <integer>]:
        reports nets above the given fanout <integer> <optional> 
    [-max_fanout <integer>]:
        reports nets below the given fanout <integer> <optional> 
    [-cap_worst <integer>]:
        reports the worst 'N' number of nets 
    [-sort <string>]:
        sort based on 'loads', 'capacitance' or 'resistance' 
    [-flat]:
        report flat net information 
    [<inst|hinst|hnet>+]:
        net or instance name(s) to report nets <optional> 

==================================================
COMMAND: report_obj
==================================================
  report_obj: reports object's attribute information 

Usage: report_obj [-help] [<string>] [<string>] [-categories <string>] [-all] [-computed] [-settable] [-tcl] [-verbose]

    [-help]:
        prints out the command usage 
    [<string>]:
        returns attributes for the given object(s) (defaults to root:) 
    [<string>]:
        only return attribute names which match the pattern (is * by default) 
    [-categories <string>]:
        returns attributes which are included in the supplied list of categories. Use a '*' to sort all attributes by category 
    [-all]:
        reports all non-computed attributes and their current value which could be default or not ('is_computed' false) 
    [-computed]:
        includes all attributes marked 'is_computed' in the data model 
    [-settable]:
        reports all attributes marked 'is_settable' in the data model and are non-default 
    [-tcl]:
        returns the objects and their changed default value as a TCL dictionary (list of lists) 
    [-verbose]:
        includes the objects data type and default value in the return (cannot be used with the -tcl option) 

