==================================================
COMMAND: report_scan_registers
==================================================
  report_scan_registers: reports DFT status of registers 

Usage: report_scan_registers [-pass_tdrc] [-fail_tdrc] [-lockup] [-latch] [-dont_scan] [-other] [-shift_register] [-multi_bit] [-test_clock <test_clock>] [-not_in_scan_chain]
           [-test_clock_edge <string>] [<design>] [> file]

    [-pass_tdrc]:
        report registers that pass TDRC 
    [-fail_tdrc]:
        report registers that fail TDRC 
    [-lockup]:
        report registers used as lockup elements 
    [-latch]:
        report level sensitive registers 
    [-dont_scan]:
        report registers marked preserved or dont_scan 
    [-other]:
        report misc. registers 
    [-shift_register]:
        report registers that are part of shift register segments 
    [-multi_bit]:
        report registers that are implemented as multibit 
    [-test_clock <test_clock>]:
        report number of flops for the test clock 
    [-not_in_scan_chain]:
        report registers that pass dft rule checks and are not a part of scan chains 
    [-test_clock_edge <string>]:
        report number of flops for the test clock edge 'rise' or 'fall' (default: rise) 
    [<design>]:
        design to report on 

