==================================================
COMMAND: set_timing_derate
==================================================

Usage: set_timing_derate [-early] [-late] [-rise] [-fall] [-clock] [-data] [-mean] [-sigma] [-net_delay] [-cell_delay] [-cell_check] [-add] [-multiply] [-input_switching]
           [-incremental_adjust] [-dynamic] [-static] [-delay_corner <delay_corner>] [-power_domain <power_domain>] <float> [<design|lib_cell|inst|hnet|hinst>+]

    [-early]:
        apply to early mode 
    [-late]:
        apply to late mode 
    [-rise]:
        apply value to rise delays 
    [-fall]:
        apply value to fall delays 
    [-clock]:
        apply to clock paths 
    [-data]:
        apply to data paths 
    [-mean]:
        apply separate derating value to the mean components of the delay 
    [-sigma]:
        apply separate derating value to the sigma components of the delay 
    [-net_delay]:
        apply to net delays 
    [-cell_delay]:
        apply to cell delays 
    [-cell_check]:
        apply to constraint arcs 
    [-add]:
        add derate to existing derate value 
    [-multiply]:
        multiply derate to existing derate value 
    [-input_switching]:
        derate as Simultaneous Switching Input derate applicable to early paths only 
    [-incremental_adjust]:
        incremental apply the derate value 
    [-dynamic]:
        apply to delta net delays only (not supported used in write_sdc) 
    [-static]:
        apply to non-delta net delays 
    [-delay_corner <delay_corner>]:
        apply to this delay corner 
    [-power_domain <power_domain>]:
        apply to this power domain 
    <float>:
        derating value 
    [<design|lib_cell|inst|hnet|hinst>+]:
        objects 

