Usage: time_info [-report] [-current] [-table <string>] [-stamp] [-save <string>] [-load <string>] [<string>]

    [-report]:
        report all stages up to this point 
    [-current]:
        report current stage 
    [-table <string>]:
        metrics table ID to support multiple tables (default is 'default') 
    [-stamp]:
        create a time stamp 
    [-save <string>]:
        name of '.tstamp' file to save runtime metrics to 
    [-load <string>]:
        name of '.tstamp' file to load runtime metrics from 
    [<string>]:
        stage name 

Note that time_info also provides a shortcut syntax where
'-report' and '-stamp' are implied. When using such syntax

> time_info STAGE_6

is equivalent to

> time_info -stamp STAGE_6 -report


