COMMAND: write_dft_pmbist_testbench
==================================================
  write_dft_pmbist_testbench: writes out data and script files to generate PMBIST patterns with 'create_embedded_test', and script files and patterns for NC simulation 

Usage: write_dft_pmbist_testbench [-create_embedded_test_options <string>] [-irun_options <string>] [-sim_options <string>] [-directory <string>] [-test_pattern_directory <string>]
           [-testbench_directory <string>] [-ncsim_library <string>] [-script_only] [-no_deposit_script] [-deposit_all_flops] [-sim_with_deposit_script] [-sim_without_assertions]
           [-no_build_model] [-build_model_netlist <string>] [-rtl] [-create_fcu_patterns] [-aux_source <string>] [-aux_top <string>] [-add_asu_testbench] [-amu_instance <hinst>]
           [-fcu_instance <hinst>] [<design>]

    [-create_embedded_test_options <string>]:
        options to pass to the create_embedded_test command (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>"). The default options are to generate bypass and production patterns 
        (-createpatterns bypass,production) if MBIST is controlled by JTAG and directaccess/burnin patterns (-createpatterns directaccess,burnin) if MBIST is controlled by direct access 
        pins in parallel parallel schedules. 
    [-irun_options <string>]:
        options to pass to the generated irun scripts (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-sim_options <string>]:
        options to pass to the generated simulation scripts (example "-option1 <string> -option2 <string>") 
    [-directory <string>]:
        output directory for scripts, test data and abstract model 
    [-test_pattern_directory <string>]:
        output directory for TBDpatt files, assign files and mode initialization files 
    [-testbench_directory <string>]:
        output directory for mbist testbench files 
    [-ncsim_library <string>]:
        list of files for NCSIM, e.g. "file1 file2" 
    [-script_only]:
        generate scripts only 
    [-no_deposit_script]:
        do not generate the deposit script that is used during simulation 
    [-deposit_all_flops]:
        deposit a value on all flops in the deposit script 
    [-sim_with_deposit_script]:
        run simulation using a deposit script 
    [-sim_without_assertions]:
        run simulation using assertions 
    [-no_build_model]:
        do not execute the build_model command 
    [-build_model_netlist <string>]:
        netlist to use for build_model 
    [-rtl]:
        target rtl design 
    [-create_fcu_patterns]:
        create FCU patterns (valid when add_hard_repair has been run) 
    [-aux_source <string>]:
        list of auxiliary design files for simulation, e.g. "mod1.v mod2.v" 
    [-aux_top <string>]:
        list of auxiliary top level design modules for simulation, e.g. "mod1 mod2" 
    [-add_asu_testbench]:
        enable generation of the ASU Verilog driver for testing on demand functions 
    [-amu_instance <hinst>]:
        name of the associated algorithm memory unit instance 
    [-fcu_instance <hinst>]:
        name of the associated fuse control unit instance 
    [<design>]:
        the name of the design 

