COMMAND: write_sv_wrapper
==================================================
  write_sv_wrapper: writes out a wrapper SystemVerilog module for a design. Such a wrapper module helps in doing comparative simulation of output netlist versus input RTL design, especially 
                    when the design description in input RTL has complex ports. 

Usage: write_sv_wrapper [-continue_on_error] [-wrapper_name <string>] [-module_name <string>] [-rename_module] [-exclude_type_definition] [<design|module>] [> file]

    [-continue_on_error]:
        do not return an error code even if the command did not execute properly 
    [-wrapper_name <string>]:
        name of wrapper module 
    [-module_name <string>]:
        name of module instantiated in wrapper 
    [-rename_module]:
        rename module in internal database with the new name (given with -module_name) 
    [-exclude_type_definition]:
        do not write (as part of wrapper) definition of complex types that are used in definition of wrapper 
    [<design|module>]:
        design or module 

