==================================================
COMMAND: vfind
==================================================
 vfind: finds an object by type and name

Usage: vfind [<root_path>] [-maxdepth <integer>] [-mindepth <integer>] [-ignorecase] [-invert <expression>] [-regexp <expression>] [-split] [-vname] [-option|*]+ <object> 

    [<root_path>]: 
        specifies the name of the directory from where to start searching. Do an explicit search if not specified. Argument may include wildcard ('*') characters. 
    <object>: 
        specifies the name of the object to match. Argument may include wildcard ('*') characters and single character match ('?') characters. 
    [-maxdepth <integer>]: 
        descends no more than the specified number of levels below 'root_path'. A level of '0' searches only the 'root_path'. Default: infinity. 
    [-mindepth <integer>]: 
        skips the specified number of levels below 'root_path' before finding objects. A level of '1' searches all objects except 'root_path'. Default: 0. 
    [-ignorecase]: 
        specifies case insensitive search 
    [-split]: 
        split output one object per line 
    [-invert <expression>]: 
        exclude objects specified by regular expression 
    [-regexp <expression>]: 
        specifies regular expression 
    [-vname]: 
        return Verilog style names where appropriate 
    [-option]: 
        specifies the type of object to find. Multiple types are supported or '*' for all. Each specified option must be of the form '-<object_type>'. The following are valid object types: 

        actual_scan_chain                  fpobject                             level_shifter_group                  opcg_trigger                         route_rule 
        actual_scan_segment                fuse_cell                            level_shifter_rule                   opcond                               route_type 
        analysis_view                      fuse_cell_domain                     lib_arc                              operating_condition                  row 
        arc                                gcell                                lib_cell                             osc_source                           scan_chain 
        attribute                          gcell_grid                           lib_pin                              osc_source_reference                 scan_segment 
        base_cell                          group                                library                              pcell                                sdp_column 
        base_cell_set                      hdl_architecture                     library_domain                       pdomain                              sdp_group 
        base_pin                           hdl_bind                             library_set                          pg_base_pin                          sdp_instance 
        blackbox                           hdl_block                            macro_isolation_rule                 pg_hnet                              sdp_row 
        blockage                           hdl_component                        macro_model                          pg_hport                             seq_function 
        boundary_scan_segment              hdl_configuration                    macro_power_domain                   pg_lib_pin                           site 
        bump                               hdl_implementation                   mbist_clock                          pg_net                               slot 
        cell                               hdl_inst                             mbist_clock_domain                   pg_pin                               specialnet 
        cell_model                         hdl_label                            memory_bank_structure                pg_port                              state_retention_rule 
        clock                              hdl_lib                              memory_data_bit_structure            pin                                  style 
        cluster                            hdl_operator                         memory_lib_cell                      pin_bus                              tap_port 
        command                            hdl_package                          memory_lib_pin_access                pinstance                            test_bus_interface 
        command_option                     hdl_parameter                        memory_lib_pin_action                place_blockage                       test_bus_port 
        congestion_box                     hdl_pin                              memory_lib_pin_alias                 pmbist_port                          test_clock 
        constant                           hdl_procedure                        memory_lib_pin_test                  pnet                                 test_clock_domain 
        constraint_mode                    hdl_subprogram                       memory_library_domain                port                                 test_signal 
        cost_group                         hinst                                memory_spare_column                  port_bus                             timing_bin 
        def_pin                            hnet                                 memory_spare_column_map_address      power_domain                         timing_bin_path 
        delay_corner                       hpin                                 memory_spare_column_map_data         power_intent_command                 timing_condition 
        design                             hpin_bus                             memory_spare_row                     power_intent_command_id              timing_path 
        dft_configuration_mode             hport                                memory_spare_row_map_address         power_mode                           timing_point 
        domain_macro_parameter             hport_bus                            message                              power_model                          track_pattern 
        exception                          inst                                 message_group                        power_scope                          via 
        external_delay                     isolation_rule                       module                               programmable_direct_access_function  violation 
        extraction_grid                    jtag_instruction                     net                                  rc_corner                            wireload 
        fill                               jtag_instruction_register            nominal_condition                    region                               wireload_selection 
        flow                               jtag_macro                           obj_type                             repeater_rule                        write_mask_bit 
        flow_step                          jtag_port                            opcg_domain                          root                                 formal_verification_constraint 
        layer                              opcg_mode                            route_blockage                       

==================================================
COMMAND: report_timing_summary
==================================================
  Generate a timing report

Usage: Generate a timing report [-help] [-checks <setup|drv+> {setup drv}] [-views <analysis_view+>] [-groups <cost_group+>] [-expand_views] [-expand_clocks <enum> {capture_only launch_capture}] [-sort_by <enum> {name wns tns fep}] [> <filename>]


    [-checks <setup|drv+> {setup drv}]:
        Generate a timing report for specified check types (enum setup drv +, optional)
    [-views <analysis_view+>]:
        Generate a timing report for specified analysis_views. By default all active views are analyzed. (object analysis_view +, optional)
    [-groups <cost_group+>]:
        Generate a timing report for specified cost_group(s) only. By default all cost_groups are analyzed. (object cost_group + , optional)
    [-expand_views]:
        Includes per analysis_view details (bool, optional)
    [-expand_clocks <enum> {capture_only launch_capture}]:
        Includes per capture or launch/capture clock group details. (enum capture_only launch_capture, optional)
    [-sort_by <enum> {name wns tns fep}]:
        Define order to sort views/clock/cost_groups for report generation. (enum name wns tns fep, optional)
    [> <filename>]:
        Output file (filename, optional)

