==================================================
COMMAND: report_sdb_annotation
==================================================
Usage: report_sdb_annotation [-stims <string>+] [-inputs] [-show_details <string>] [<object>] [> file]

    [-stims <string>+]:
        Report the annotation of given stims. Default: all stims.
    [-inputs]: 
        Report the annotation of inputs pins. Displays flop, memory, latch, icgc inputs. 
    [-show_details <string>]: 
        Format is <obj_type>[:<annotation_type>[:<pin_prop_type>]]  
        <obj_type> = port|port_dft|seq|comb|reg|reg_dft|mem|mem_dft|icgc|latch|bbox|pad|pm|mux|drivers|rtl_drivers|all (default: all)
        <annotation_type> = asserted|unasserted|unconnected|all (after read_stimulus and before compute_power)
                             = asserted|user_asserted|prop_asserted|computed|default|clock_source|constant|unasserted|unconnected|non_toggle|all (after compute_power or propagate_activity)
                               (default: all)
        <pin_prop_type> = in|out|clock|enable|all (default: out).
    [<object>]:
        Reports the annotation of given design/inst. Default: top design.

