==================================================
COMMAND: set_sense
==================================================

Usage: set_sense [-clocks <clock>+] [-stop_propagation] [-positive] [-negative] [-type <string>+] <arc|port|pin|hpin>+

    [-clocks <clock>+]:
        clock list 
    [-stop_propagation]:
        stops the propagation of specified clocks and data-paths from specified pins 
    [-positive]:
        specifies positive unateness with respect to clock source 
    [-negative]:
        specifies negative unateness with respect to clock source 
    [-type <string>+]:
        apply clock sense to following objects (all, clock, data, clock_source_data) 
    <arc|port|pin|hpin>+:
        objects( arc | port | pin | hpin) 

==================================================
COMMAND: set_clock_groups
==================================================

Usage: set_clock_groups [-name <string>] [-comment <string>] [-logically_exclusive] [-physically_exclusive] [-asynchronous] [-allow_paths] (-group <string>)+

    [-name <string>]:
        name of the clock group 
    [-comment <string>]:
        comment to be tagged with this command 
    [-logically_exclusive]:
        indicates that the clock groups are logically exclusive with respect to each other 
    [-physically_exclusive]:
        indicates that the clock groups are physically exclusive with respect to each other 
    [-asynchronous]:
        indicates that the clock groups are asynchronous with respect to each other 
    [-allow_paths]:
        allows timing analysis between asynchronous clock groups 
    -group <string>:
        usage is -group <clock_list_1> -group <clock_list_2> .. and so on. Atleast one -group <clock_list> is required 

