    [-max]:
        max transition 
    <float>:
        transition value 
    [<string>]:
        pin|hpin|port 

==================================================
COMMAND: reset_ideal_transition
==================================================
  reset_ideal_transition_fast: internal command for set_ideal_transition 

Usage: reset_ideal_transition_fast [-rise] [-fall] [-min] [-max] [<string>]

    [-rise]:
        rising transition 
    [-fall]:
        falling transition 
    [-min]:
        min transition 
    [-max]:
        max transition 
    [<string>]:
        pin|hpin|port 

==================================================
COMMAND: reset_ideal_latency
==================================================
  reset_ideal_latency_fast: internal command for reset_ideal_latency 

Usage: reset_ideal_latency_fast [-rise] [-fall] [-min] [-max] [<string>]

    [-rise]:
        rising latency 
    [-fall]:
        falling latency 
    [-min]:
        min latency 
    [-max]:
        max latency 
    [<string>]:
        pin|hpin|port 

==================================================
COMMAND: set_mode
==================================================

Usage: set_mode [-type <string>] <string> <inst|hinst>

    [-type <string>]:
        specify the liberty cell type of the instance 
    <string>:
        mode value 
    <inst|hinst>:
        instance object 

==================================================
COMMAND: set_path_adjust
==================================================
  path_adjust: adjusts path constraints for timing analysis 

Usage: path_adjust [-from <inst|hinst|external_delay|clock|port|pin|hpin>+] [-through <inst|hinst|port|pin|hpin>+]+ [-to <inst|hinst|external_delay|clock|port|pin|hpin>+] [-paths <string>]
           [-view <analysis_view>] -delay <delay in picoseconds> [-setup] [-hold] [-name <string>]

    [-from <inst|hinst|external_delay|clock|port|pin|hpin>+]:
        from list 
    [-through <inst|hinst|port|pin|hpin>+]:
        specifies paths that pass through these pins or instances. This option can be repeated indicating that the path must go through at least one element of each through list (in the 
        order the options were specified). Objects must be ports, hierarchical pins, pins on sequential/mapped combinational cells, or sequential/mapped combinational instances 
    [-to <inst|hinst|external_delay|clock|port|pin|hpin>+]:
        to list 
    [-paths <string>]:
        a path identifier result from the specify_paths command 
    [-view <analysis_view>]:
        an analysis_view the paths should be restricted to 
    -delay <delay in picoseconds>:
        delay adjust value 
    [-setup]:
        exception is for setup timing analysis only (default is both setup and hold) 
    [-hold]:
        exception is for hold timing analysis only (default is both setup and hold) 
    [-name <string>]:
        exception name 

