==================================================
COMMAND: external_delay
==================================================
  noop15: specifies delay that is outside the design 

Usage: noop15 ( -input <delay {r f R F} in picoseconds> | -output <delay {r f R F} in picoseconds> ) [-sigma_delay <float>+] [-mode <mode>] [-clock <clock>+]
           [ -edge_rise |
             -edge_fall ] [-level_sensitive] [-accumulate] [-name <string>] <pin|hpin|port>+

    -input <delay {r f R F} in picoseconds>:
        clock to input valid time 
    -output <delay {r f R F} in picoseconds>:
        output valid to clock time 
    [-sigma_delay <float>+]:
        sigma delay for socv analysis 
    [-mode <mode>]:
        the mode for the external delay 
    [-clock <clock>+]:
        clock object 
    [-edge_rise]:
        rise clock edge 
    [-edge_fall]:
        fall clock edge 
    [-level_sensitive]:
        external event is level-sensitive 
    [-accumulate]:
        allows more than one external delay per clock per phase (default=false) 
    [-name <string>]:
        external delay name 
    <pin|hpin|port>+:
        object(s) 

